UPDATE public.stories SET title = '👁️ This Exercises Improves Your Vision 🔍 1. Near-Far Focus Activity 	•	This exercise is like push-ups for your eyes, strengthening your focusing system. 	•	How to do it: 	•	Cover one eye with your hand. 	•	Hold a finger, pen, or pencil in front of your uncovered eye. 	•	Slowly bring it closer until it becomes slightly blurry, then stop and refocus to make it clear. 	•	Hold focus for 5 seconds, visualizing your pupil locking in and getting smaller. 	•	Shift your focus to a distant point as far as possible. Relax your focus and hold for 5 seconds. 	•	Alternate between near and far focus for a few minutes. 	•	Repeat with the other eye. 🔄 Why it works: 	•	It activates and relaxes the focusing muscles in your eyes, improving near and far vision flexibility. 🧠 Tip: Consistency is key. Treat this like a workout for your eyes to see gradual improvement over time. 🗣️ Speakers: Dave Asprey, Dr. Bryce Appelbaum 🎵 Music: Linkin Park - One More Light 🎬 Video: Dave Asprey (YouTube) Contact us for credit or removal requests (no copyright intended) ©️ All rights and credits reserved to the respective owner(s).' WHERE slug = 'tiktok-7458502073160584456';
