UPDATE public.stories SET title = 'Children who do chores aren’t just helping out around the house—they’re building skills that will benefit them for life. Studies show that kids who take on age-appropriate chores tend to be more successful and happier as they grow up. Why? Because chores do more than teach responsibility. They help build a child’s self-esteem, showing them that they’re capable of contributing in a meaningful way. Each completed task, whether it’s making the bed or setting the table, gives them a sense of accomplishment and boosts their confidence. By learning these skills early on—starting even as young toddlers—children gain independence and a sense of purpose that will carry them into adulthood with resilience and confidence. Audio: @CubstoBears ' WHERE slug = 'tiktok-7423837301077462318';
