UPDATE public.stories SET title = 'Top 4 pickleball drills to improve your control and coordination ✅ 1. The Sky Lob. Hit the ball as high as you can and attempt to “catch” it with your paddle. This will work on your hand-eye coordination and your paddle control. Make sure to get some reps with your backhand side as well.  2. The Spin Bounce. Bounce the ball on your paddle, but incorporate spin both ways. This works on your touch and spin.  3. The Karate Chop. Bounce the ball on the floor by hitting with your paddle edge. Because the edge is much thinner, this will work on your coordination a bit more.  4. Paddle Roll. Roll the ball back and forth between your forehand and backhand side. This works on your paddle coordination and control.  - Btw, if you’re wondering why my grip looks different, I’m using a Hesacore grip. It’s like a contoured grip that fits your hand like a glove for an ergonomic feel. It’s a game changer. Link in my bio @hesacore_pickleball  – 👉 follow @davispickleball for daily tips, drills and more . . . . . #pickleballislife #pickleball #pickleballtips #pickleballaddiction #davispickleball #selkirksport #wearepickleball' WHERE slug = 'tiktok-7291702726105271595';
