UPDATE public.stories SET title = 'Musicians of tiktok, performance videos are still a solid way to go to promote your music. You can usually get a more out of them than just a few posts. ‘Performance videos’ in this case refers to the mini music video style posts we’re so used to seeing now, not live performances—you don’t have to go out and book shows to make this happen :) If you have 5 different full length music performance vids, and you can squeeze ten shorter vids out of each, you’re setting up yourself for about 2 months of content for one song, or 1 month going hard on the posts. And this doesn’t have to be your entire strategy either. Add in some stories, any other content you think would be cool, and a lot of engagement with people on the platforms and you’ll probably get a decent response overall (if the music is good). A blend of unity and variety is a good thing. This method lends itself to both. To keep things interesting enough you can use different sections of the song, different length clips, try different hooks or text among them, and alternate between all the different performances you did. You could also take a few different outfits to add more variety.  You’ll hopefully find bits of the song that do better than others on here, and you can lean more into those to maximise your efforts.  Yes, it will annoy some people—that’s fine. Your art is worth pushing hard, right? Remember this is just one way to go and you don’t have to do this. You always have a choice :) #musicmarketing #indieartisttips #independentartistsoftiktok #musiciansoftiktok ' WHERE slug = 'tiktok-7272313686017035538';
