UPDATE public.stories SET title = 'This hits hard. They are talking about why we should discipline ourselves, why we should take chances, why we should take more action and do things we are afraid of. One life. One life that does not care about your regrets. He beautifully articulated something that has always haunted me. But it’s his passion that got me. This is Eric Weinstein is a podcast host, and modern day philosopher (in my book) who has some amazing ideas and difficult discussions. This clip is from the @triggerpod podcast. Amazing episode. You may not agree with some of his ideas, but you can’t be so ignorant to disregard a rant like this because of it. That last quote: “Back then we didn’t realize it was just music.” So beautiful. But so scary. The idea that it’s really up to us to figure out how to subscribe meaning to every moment in our lives. Something our entire society has seem to forgotten how to do. I hope this clip helps at least one of you make the change. Love you all. #ericweinstein #triggernometry #philosophy #philosophyquotes #procrastination #regret #motivation #nevergiveup #lifehacks #cinema #filmisnotdead #indiefilm #filmmaking #screenwriter #screenwriting ' WHERE slug = 'tiktok-7250348954200673582';
UPDATE public.stories SET title = 'According to John Gottman, it''s crucial for a couple to honor each other''s dreams because it strengthens the emotional connection and fosters a sense of support and understanding within the relationship. When we respect and value our partner''s dreams, we show them that we genuinely care about their happiness and fulfillment. It''s like saying, "Hey, I''m here for you, and I want to help you achieve your dreams because they matter to you." To learn about each other''s dreams and honor them, here are a few steps you can take: Create a safe space: Set aside time to have open and non-judgmental conversations where both of you can express your dreams freely. Remember, it''s essential to listen without interrupting or criticizing. Ask open-ended questions: Encourage your partner to share their aspirations by asking questions like, "What are some things you''ve always wanted to do or achieve?" or "If you could pursue any dream, what would it be?" These questions give them the freedom to explore their desires. Show genuine interest: As your partner shares their dreams, actively engage in the conversation. Ask follow-up questions and show enthusiasm for their ideas. This demonstrates that you value their dreams and want to understand them better. Offer support and encouragement: Once you know your partner''s dreams, be their cheerleader. Encourage them to pursue their passions and provide the support they need along the way. Gottman says, "We can be a dream-catcher for our partner by helping to facilitate their lifelong dreams." Collaborate and compromise: Sometimes, your dreams and your partner''s dreams may not perfectly align. In such cases, find common ground and seek compromise. Work together to create a shared vision that honors both of your aspirations. Remember, the key is to approach this process with kindness, empathy, and an open mind. By honoring each other''s dreams, you can build a stronger, more fulfilling relationship. As Gottman puts it, "Marriage is a journey of exploration and shared dreams, where kindness, love, and support form the foundation for a lifetime of mutual growth and happiness." #therapytok #therapistsontiktok #gottmanmethod #gottmaninstitute ' WHERE slug = 'tiktok-7232320990494084395';
