UPDATE public.stories SET title = 'Sound is the source of all creation. Sound gives form, sound gives life. There is a mind blowing video on YouTube where a guy makes his car waves with some specific frequencies, and also a video where a Bridge waves massively because of the frequency it was on, it would match the frequency of the wind and it started to wave till it collapsed.  Source of the video (Title on YouTube): Michio Kaku Explains Multiverse, Aliens & Quantum IMMORTALITY | 145 Summary of the Podcast:  This podcast with the physicist Michio Kaku discuss three fascinating topics: the multiverse, aliens, and quantum immortality. Here''s a breakdown of what each topic generally entails: Multiverse: Michio Kaku explores the concept of the multiverse, which suggests the existence of multiple universes beyond our own. He delves into theories such as the inflationary multiverse and the many-worlds interpretation of quantum mechanics. The discussion likely covers the possibility of parallel universes, different laws of physics, and the potential implications of a multiverse for our understanding of reality. Aliens: In this part of the podcast, Michio Kaku delves into the topic of extraterrestrial life. He might discuss the likelihood of intelligent life existing elsewhere in the universe, the search for extraterrestrial intelligence (SETI), and the potential implications of discovering alien civilizations. This could involve discussing various theories on how life might evolve on other planets and the technological advancements necessary for interstellar communication or travel. Quantum Immortality: Michio Kaku explores the concept of quantum immortality, a thought experiment rooted in quantum mechanics. It proposes that conscious observers could experience a form of immortality through the multiverse. The discussion might involve topics such as the role of observation in quantum theory, the relationship between consciousness and reality, and the philosophical implications of quantum immortality. Overall, this podcast episode offers a fascinating exploration of these speculative and thought-provoking topics from the perspective of a renowned physicist like Michio Kaku. #epigenetictips ' WHERE slug = 'tiktok-7233899168970935598';
